# Build output.
#
# `bin/` is not ignored wholesale any more, because one file in it is now source: the
# launcher `/colai:show` reaches on PATH. Everything a build drops beside it still is.
bin/*
!bin/colai-toolbar

dist/
node_modules/
toolbar/src-tauri/target/

# Where `clawhub package pack` puts the tarball it uploads. It is the build output again,
# 5 MB of it, and committing one would put a stale copy of the plugin in the repository
# people read to check what the plugin is.
.pack/

# The shipped toolbar, per machine.
#
# The archive is tracked and the binary is not, which looks backwards and is not: this is
# what a `claude plugin install` receives, and Claude Code runs nothing at install time. If
# the toolbar is not in the clone, it is nowhere — there is no later step that fetches it.
# So the 5 MB archive travels, the 13 MB binary it unpacks to does not, and the digest
# beside it is what says they are the same thing.
platforms/*/bin/*
!platforms/*/bin/colai-toolbar.gz
!platforms/*/bin/colai-toolbar.sha256
!platforms/*/bin/colai-toolbar.build.json
